    3. Build the rounded-rectangle mask from parameters (rows widen by 2 per step from edge).
    4. Place objects on grid ensuring bboxes don't overlap and have >= 2 cell gap.
       Allow at least one object to be near a grid edge so some caps get clipped.
    5. Verify yellow caps from different objects don't overlap (reject if so).
    6. Foreground color = random non-yellow, non-black color.
